# Walkthrough: Advanced Bot Recording & Randomization

I have successfully implemented your advanced bot flow, focusing on high-speed "Bulk Recording" and human-like "Randomization."

## New Features

### 1. 🎙 Bulk Mouse Recording
You no longer need to click "Add Click" for every single spot.
- Click the new **🎙 Record Sequence** button.
- The window will hide, and **every click** you perform on the screen will be instantly saved as a new step.
- When you are finished, just press the **ESC** key to return to the configuration.
- All your clicks (body, tabs, etc.) will be automatically added to the sequence list!

### 2. 🎲 Random Choice Groups
As requested, I've added a **"Random Sequence Window"** feature.
- Use the **🎲 Add Random Choice** button.
- It will ask you to label the group (e.g. "Pick Random Link").
- You can then record two different positions.
- During playback, the bot will **randomly pick one** of those two positions to click, making the bot behave more like a human and less predictably.

### 3. Automatic "Return to App" (Alt+Tab)
The looping logic has been refined:
- If your sequence switches from **Brave** to an **IDE**, the bot will Alt+Tab to the IDE.
- When the sequence loops back to the start, the bot will **automatically switch back to Brave** before the first click.
- This ensures your multi-window workflow is completely seamless.

## How to use Bulk Recording
1. Set your target window (e.g., Brave).
2. Click **🎙 Record Sequence**.
3. Click all the places you want the bot to go.
4. Press **ESC**.
5. See your entire sequence populated in one go!

Everything is ready for you to start building complex, multi-window loops.
